# Project core

Desktop-first Vite/React/TS. Prefer the existing layering; do not invent parallel
math or lesson pipelines.

## Layers

The layer table is owned by
[docs/engineering/architecture.md](../../docs/engineering/architecture.md) —
read it there, do not restate it. The rule it enforces: math lives only in
`src/math`, guided scenes receive a `guidedSceneId` (React never imports a scene
module), explorers register in `registry.tsx`, and the lesson shell never
branches per lesson.

## Scope

- The **built surface** is whatever `src/lessons/courseModel.ts` marks
  `kind: "lesson"`. Read it from the file; never trust a copy in a doc.
- Nodes marked `kind: "future"` are **closed to implementation**. Promoting one
  (`future → built`) or writing its lesson code is an approval boundary —
  see [AGENTS.md § Approval boundaries](../../AGENTS.md), which owns those rules.
- Prefer fixing visual/math correctness and shared helpers over new lesson content.
- Any course or lesson authoring request routes through
  [docs/authoring/course-authoring-workflow.md](../../docs/authoring/course-authoring-workflow.md) first.

## Math & copy

- Learner-facing math uses KaTeX (`ProseWithMath`, equation/readout components),
  including MC choices when they are matrices/vectors.
- Prefer `matrixVectorMultiply` / shared helpers over ad-hoc formulas in UI code.

## Browser review screenshots

Save app screenshots **only** under `screenshots/` (gitignored), always via an
absolute path such as `/home/thomas/Dev/technical-learning/screenshots/<name>.png`.
Never write captures to the home directory or Downloads.
